WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:00.832
The job.

2
00:00:01.112 --> 00:00:10.029
Every week, someone on a product team reads the issue tracker and writes a status update: what shipped, what is blocked, what slipped, what needs a decision.

3
00:00:10.309 --> 00:00:15.515
It takes an hour if the tracker is tidy, and it is the kind of work people do late on Friday.

4
00:00:15.795 --> 00:00:27.208
Your studio project automates it: an agent that reads a tracker through an MCP server you build, drafts the weekly status, and posts it only after a person approves the draft.

5
00:00:27.488 --> 00:00:34.080
You will evaluate it on at least 15 scenarios, including injection attempts, and report what each run costs.

6
00:00:34.360 --> 00:00:36.003
This lesson does not build it.

7
00:00:36.283 --> 00:00:47.205
It walks through the decisions you need to make first, in the order a careful engineer would make them, so that by the end of the week your design document can answer the questions a reviewer will ask.

8
00:00:47.485 --> 00:00:51.432
The project page has the requirements, rubric, and write-up template.
